# No trailing slash. "node_modules/" matches a directory and not a symlink of
# that name, which is what a worktree has if you link the install rather than
# repeat it - so the link goes into the next commit, silently. `npm install` in
# the worktree avoids it too, but the pattern should not be the thing that has
# to be remembered.
node_modules
.claude/

# Local wrangler state - the emulated KV, D1, R2 and cache stores, and tmp.
# It is in .assetsignore as well, and the two are not the same job: that file
# stops it being served, this one stops it being committed by an `add -A`
# after somebody has run `wrangler dev`.
.wrangler
